content:
=== HYPOTHESIS ===
# p_a3c7 — Priya's desk is desk_b1, not the office (fork of p_e5f6)

The parent document predicted that Priya's headphones and pen would be at desk_o1 on weekday afternoons (10:00–14:00), treating the office as her music and study space. Two looks at desk_o1 in that window found neither object, and the per-object statistics confirm both headphones_priya and pen_priya at desk_b1 on every sighted day (2/2 days, 1 receptacle each). This fork removes the "office as creative workspace" claim entirely.

Priya's headphones and pen stay at desk_b1 (the bedroom desk) around the clock. The office (desk_o1) holds only plant_pot_3 and, occasionally, the speaker for ambient sound. Elena commutes all five weekdays (8:00–17:30) with laptop, backpack, wallet, hat, jacket, keys, and umbrella out of the house. Her helmet and bike lock remain at the entry (she walks to a transit stop, not cycling). Priya is home most of the day: morning walk 7–8, afternoon errands 14–16. The dog is fed by Priya at 7:30 (bowl at kitchen floor) and walked by Elena at 18:00. Meals at the dining table: lunch 12:00–13:30, dinner 18:30–20:00. Evening TV 20:30–22:30 with remote and blanket on the coffee table. Guitar in the bedroom for evening practice (19–21), living room on weekend afternoons.

What changed from the parent: the weekday 10–14 blocks placing headphones_priya and pen_priya at desk_o1 are removed; both objects now have a single all-day block at desk_b1. The speaker's weekday office block is removed. The four claims are updated to test desk_b1 rather than desk_o1.

What would refute this fork: headphones_priya or pen_priya sighted at desk_o1 on a weekday afternoon, or the office desk regularly holding more than the plant and speaker.

