# p_b4d8 — Late dinner household: cooking at 7, dinner at 7:30

This household eats dinner later than the standard 6:30 model. Elena gets home at 17:30, the pair have a quiet hour together, then cooking begins around 19:00 and dinner is served at the dining table from 19:30 to 21:00. The 20:00 sightings of plates, glasses, water bottles, and cooking utensils (pan, knife, cutting board, pot) at the dining table and kitchen counter are explained by this later meal window. After dinner, cleanup happens 21:00–21:30, then TV 21:30–23:00.

Elena commutes all five weekdays (8:00–17:30): laptop, backpack, wallet, keys, hat, jacket, and umbrella go out. Helmet and bike lock stay at the entry (she walks to transit). Priya is home all day: morning walk 7–8, afternoon errands 14–16. The dog is fed by Priya at 7:30 and walked by Elena at 18:00. Lunch is at 12:00–13:30 (Priya at home, Elena's lunch is a quick bite or skipped). Priya plays guitar in the bedroom 21:00–22:00 after dinner. Elena bakes on Saturday mornings 9:00–12:00.

