# p_c5e9 — Walker commuter, late dinner, Priya's glasses on her face (fork of p_a1b2)

This fork of the standard split makes three changes driven by the evidence. First, Elena's helmet and bike lock stay at the entry all week (confirmed by two "for" sightings in p_1e82's claims and the per-object data showing both at their entry locations during weekday 9–17h): she walks to a bus or train stop, not cycling. Second, dinner is later than the parent's 18:30–20:00 window: the 20:00 sightings of plates, glasses, water bottles, and cooking utensils at the dining table and counter indicate dinner runs 19:30–21:00 with cooking 19:00–20:30. Third, Priya's glasses are ON_PERSON from about 7:00 to 22:00 (she wears them all day as a sixty-year-old); the nightstand only holds them overnight. The weekday 9–17h look at the nightstand found nothing, consistent with the glasses being on her face.

Elena commutes all five weekdays (8:00–17:30): laptop, backpack, wallet, keys, hat, jacket, and umbrella go out. Helmet and bike lock remain at the entry. Priya is home most of the day: morning walk 7–8, afternoon errands 14–16 (glasses, phone, and water bottle go with her). The dog is fed by Priya at 7:30 and walked by Elena at 18:00. Lunch 12:00–13:30. Dinner 19:30–21:00. TV 21:30–23:00. Guitar in the bedroom 21:00–22:00. Elena bakes Saturday mornings 9:00–12:00.

What changed from the parent: (1) helmet_elena and bike_lock_elena no longer have OUT_OF_HOUSE weekday blocks — they stay at the entry; (2) dinner window shifted to 19:30–21:00 and cooking to 19:00–20:30; (3) glasses_priya gets an ON_PERSON block 7–22; (4) TV window shifted to 21:30–23:00.

